<Section Class="p-0" Size="HeadingSize.H4" Name="ChartTimeValue" PageUrl="@pageUrl" Link="chart-time-value">
    <Block>
        A <code>ChartTimeValue</code> is a date or a date and time on a time axis. It has no properties to set: assign a .NET date value and it converts implicitly.
        <div class="content">
            <ul>
                <li><code>DateOnly</code>: a wall-clock date, shown as the same calendar date in every browser time zone.</li>
                <li><code>DateTime</code>: a value of kind <code>Unspecified</code> is a wall-clock time, shown the same in every browser time zone; a value of kind <code>Utc</code> or <code>Local</code> is an exact instant, and a <code>Local</code> value is converted with the time zone of the .NET process.</li>
                <li><code>DateTimeOffset</code>: an exact instant, shown in the browser's local time.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        It is the item type of <code>ChartData.TimeLabels</code>, the type of <code>ChartTimePoint.X</code>, and the type of the axis limits <code>ChartAxes.MinTime</code>, <code>MaxTime</code>, <code>SuggestedMinTime</code> and <code>SuggestedMaxTime</code>.
    </Block>
</Section>

